  "notes": "The hinge the research names — between the Gucci-era chant and the Thug-orbit sung flow — and the parameter that carries it is the melody, not the drums. \"The vocal is the melody engine — long sustained notes, wide leaps into falsetto, moderate-to-high syllable density with sung tails\" is `articulation: legato` with `intervals.leap` 0.3 and `octaveJumpProb` 0.32, which is the leapiest sung line in this batch against 2 Chainz's repeated-interval motif at the other end. `dorian` is authored beside `natural_minor` because the research names it and because \"hooks orbit the ♭3 and 5\" is a modal claim rather than a functional one — `colorTones` carries that. The 808 \"tracks the sung melody's root motion\" with a \"frequent up-glide into the bar\", which is `followsLeadRoot` with slides positioned on the bar lines and a `M2`/`P4` interval set rather than the octave. Hats are triplet-based and \"thicken under hooks\": `8T` at `fillDensity` 0.6. ⚠ **[LOW-CONF] on the kick grammar**, marked as such in the research; `syncopation` 0.58 spread across the bar's 16ths is that claim. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` — flow and era are well attested, production specifics generalized. ⚠ `followsLeadRoot` is authored intent the engine does not read yet; it is named because \"tracking the sung melody's root motion\" is the entry's most specific 808 claim and dropping it would lose it. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the three-deep clap as a layer offset, and the family weights. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
